... 'not runnable over an inline eval fixture')`","passes.py:502 — ISF findings stamp `\"cohort\": [\"ISF\"]`; container_stage.py:73 / passes.py:443 stamp a container cohort, so both classes ARE present in the mined `cohort` sets the selector reads","Plan describes only a single fixture shape: '.rebar/evals/<prompt-id>.eval.yaml' with a plan transcribed to `expect: pass`/`fail`; no per-class (container `children` / ISF session-log) branch or skip is specified","Locational note: the plan cites `sidecar.py:650-716` and `passes.py:284,291-297`, but the file is `plan_review/sidecar.py` and the cache/instructions checkpoint code is at `pass1.py:283-298` (passes.py has no matching lines); substantive claims still reproduce"],"finding":"The plan's fixture emitter and no-fire predicate assume every mined criterion is runnable over an inline-text `expect: pass`/`fail` fixture, but the eval solver has three criterion-class-keyed runner paths: container criteria (G3/G4/decomp-shape, `CONTAINER_CRITERIA`) require a `children` list payload with `input` as the parent plan, and ISF finders RAISE on any inline fixture (they need a session log). Both classes carry a `cohort` tag in the sidecar, so the generic selector admits them as fire/no-fire candidates, yet the plan specifies no fallback for emitting or reproducing a fixture whose finder cannot consume inline plan text.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f331502f60ade4b26","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach (\"Mine that corpus offline into per-criterion fire/no-fire eval fixtures\") and No-fire evidence predicate; Acceptance Criteria bullets 1 and 3","norm_id":"n792d583277524ee5","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Selector admits an in-cohort silent plan for decomp-shape (a container criterion); emitter writes an inline `expect: pass` fixture; admission run's reproduction step fails with 'needs a non-empty children list' and the criterion can never gain a spec","Selector admits a no-fire candidate for ISF; emitter transcribes an inline fixture; `rebar criteria eval` raises 'not runnable over an inline eval fixture', stalling the admission run"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In Scope/No-goals, exclude `CONTAINER_CRITERIA` (G3/G4/decomp-shape) and ISF from inline fixture mining, routing each to an `unreliable-criterion:` ticket via the self-healing loop; OR extend the emitter to produce the container `children` fixture shape and skip ISF, and have the admission runner treat an un-runnable fixture shape as a WITHHELD-with-reason rather than a hard error.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"insufficient","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add an acceptance criterion to the selector (or emitter) encoding the parent's cohort predicate: emit `expect: pass` only when C is in some finding's `cohort` on the plan AND no finding cites C, skip missing-`cohort` rows, verified by the three-shape synthetic corpus (in-cohort silent emitted, never-in-cohort skipped, missing-cohort skipped).","cohort":["G3","G4"],"criteria":["G3"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Parent AC1: 'A no-fire (`expect: pass`) case for criterion C is emitted only when C is in the `cohort` set of some finding on that plan AND no finding on that plan cites C; a row with a missing `cohort` key is skipped ... verified by `pytest` over a synthetic corpus with an in-cohort silent plan (emitted), a never-in-cohort plan (skipped), and a missing-cohort row (skipped).'","Selector approach: '*Reproduction consensus* ... The only signal valid in the no-fire direction.' and selector AC: 'A no-fire candidate never reaches `blocking`; verified by `pytest` asserting `advisory` for one holding reproduction consensus.' — no selector AC references `cohort`, in-cohort vs never-in-cohort, or missing-cohort skipping.","Child decomposition: 'No-fire predicate AC -> the selector (owns/applies the cohort + no-finding predicate) and the emitter (transcribes ...)' — but neither child's AC list encodes the cohort predicate or the three-shape corpus test.","docs/plan-review-gate.md:1457-1459 confirms `cohort` is the load-bearing routing-proof and 'missing `cohort` as unknown (skip it)'.","container pairing: parent + 092c-a664-2477-4d83/1cef-7fbc-e402-467c/5169-ab69-9c23-4f8b/549b-9cc5-940e-46c3/67aa-eb04-8814-4975/a5bf-c1f8-3950-4f87/fb55-04d6-4beb-4025"],"finding":"The parent's no-fire AC1 is stated as a cohort-membership predicate (C in the `cohort` set of some finding AND no finding cites C; a missing-`cohort` row skipped), verified by a synthetic corpus with an in-cohort silent plan, a never-in-cohort plan, and a missing-cohort row. No sibling's acceptance criteria deliver this observable outcome. The selector (549b) defines its ONLY no-fire signal as 'reproduction consensus' over equal-`material_fingerprint` pairs and never mentions `cohort` in any of its 10 ACs; the emitter (092c) 'transcribes' and tests only balance/rank/validation. The cohort predicate and its three-shape corpus test are asserted in the parent's prose but are not an acceptance criterion of any child.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f770398f519f1bb56","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"child 549b-9cc5-940e-46c3 (selector); child 092c-a664-2477-4d83 (emitter)","norm_id":"n99c64c7c8ef442e6","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A contributor implements the selector to admit a no-fire candidate on reproduction-consensus silence alone, without proving C was routed via cohort membership — precisely the ABSENCE-inference hazard the parent's Approach warns against — and the child passes all its own ACs.","The completion verifier for parent AC1 runs the three-shape synthetic-corpus test, which no child's test suite was required to implement."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Give the selector an AC that asserts the cohort predicate and the three-shape corpus outcome, so the parent AC1 verifier maps to a concrete child test rather than only to Approach prose.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"insufficient","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"insufficient","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"missing_required_child","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Assign ownership of the AC2 reconciliation script (routing key set vs `.rebar/evals/` + `src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/` + open `unreliable-criterion:` titles, exit non-zero on any gap) to a specific child and add it as that child's acceptance criterion.","cohort":["G3","G4"],"criteria":["G3"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Parent AC2: '... verified by a script that sets the routing key set against `ls .rebar/evals/ src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/` and the open-ticket titles, and exits non-zero if any criterion is in neither set.'","Self-healing loop ACs cover: already-spec'd criterion absent from attempt list; third-run breaker ticket; skipped-unbalanced counts as failure; open-ticket criterion skipped; ledger stop; cleared-env run; due-stamp interval — none states a completeness reconciliation that exits non-zero over the full routing key set.","Admission runner ACs cover admit/withhold, budget refusal, strict validity, no-shadowing, live run, discovered_from tickets — none states the criterion-set-vs-specs+tickets completeness check.","Child decomposition assigns Coverage AC to selector+emitter+admission runner+self-healing loop 'with residual gaps handled by the self-healing loop', but the loop files tickets rather than verifying the invariant.","container pairing: parent + 092c-a664-2477-4d83/1cef-7fbc-e402-467c/5169-ab69-9c23-4f8b/549b-9cc5-940e-46c3/67aa-eb04-8814-4975/a5bf-c1f8-3950-4f87/fb55-04d6-4beb-4025"],"finding":"Parent AC2 requires a reconciliation SCRIPT that computes `criteria.effective_routing(...)`'s key set against `ls .rebar/evals/ src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/` and the open `unreliable-criterion:` ticket titles and exits non-zero if any criterion is in neither set. No sibling's acceptance criteria own or commit that script. The admission runner (67aa) writes specs and the self-healing loop (1cef) files the tickets, but the loop's ACs cover only attempt-list selection, breaker ticket creation, the ledger stop, and the due-stamp — none asserts the whole-set completeness check that exits non-zero. The completeness invariant (every criterion in one set or the other) is produced piecewise but its verifier is unowned.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4dea22163a309654","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"child 1cef-7fbc-e402-467c (self-healing loop); child 67aa-eb04-8814-4975 (admission runner)","norm_id":"n390d4d4dd0e6093c","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A criterion ends up with neither a spec nor an `unreliable-criterion:` ticket (e.g. it was never attempted because the loop had not yet run, or was dropped by a selection edge case); no child's test would catch the gap because the parent AC2 verifier script is unimplemented and unowned.","The epic's completion verifier for AC2 tries to run the reconciliation script and finds it does not exist in any child's deliverables."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add the completeness-reconciliation script and its non-zero-exit AC to the self-healing loop child (which already knows the routing set and the ticket titles), or to the ADR/docs child as a committed check.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"insufficient","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_